Looking at the net, consider the vertex where four triangles meet at the point between edges C and x (the middle vertex where the left strip joins the center). Around this vertex, four faces of the net already meet in a continuous fan (the left triangle, the two middle triangles, and the downward triangle below). Since exactly four faces meet at each vertex of a folded octahedron, this fan closes up completely, forcing the two boundary edges at that vertex to be glued together. Those boundary edges are edge C (the base of the left triangle) and edge x (the blue edge). Checking the rest of the gluings (B with the unlabeled right edge, D with another edge, E with A) confirms consistency.

Therefore edge x coincides with edge C.

